WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.500
- Let's get into our conversation
with a Los Angeles native

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.490
and an incredible human being,

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.780
someone who can speak
to this city so much,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.810
she wrote a real love letter herself

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.611
to this beautiful place.

00:00:14.611 --> 00:00:15.926
It's Billie Eilish.

00:00:15.926 --> 00:00:17.710
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.030
I watched your documentary.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:25.030
I've been following you for
as long as I can remember.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.550
And there there's a moment in your concert

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.920
when you snap your ankle
and you walk off stage

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.500
and you come out and this
is one of the reasons

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.217
why I'm so in love with
you is because you say,

00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:41.670
"Look, I just want to
do it a certain way."

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.650
And people don't know how
to usually be so honest

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.760
in those moments.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.120
How do you just say it like it is?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.430
How do you know to do that?

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.410
That is such an art.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:56.880
- You know, I've always been very,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.750
very strong-willed and honest,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.080
which I think is like
a blessing and a curse.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.640
But the funny thing is that (chuckles)

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.540
the older I've gotten the
less confident I've gotten

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.520
and it kind of made me like almost...

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.530
'Cause I rewatched the
doc like a few weeks ago

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.750
and it made me cry\ because I was thinking

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.750
how like free spirited I was
and how open-minded I was,

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.490
and then it's like the media

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:31.700
just like tears it away from you.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.800
And it's like it's not fun right now

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.773
so it's like I'm trying-
- I know.

00:01:36.773 --> 00:01:40.200
- I know, I'm trying
to like, I don't know.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.810
But I'm figuring it out.
- Believe me, I get it.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:43.844
(Billie chuckling)

00:01:43.844 --> 00:01:46.820
And I have such faith that you will

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:50.210
because even when you're struggling,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.103
you're aware of the struggle.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.470
You said something that really
struck me in the documentary.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.440
You really have this issue
with the word "fans."

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.400
And I was wondering where that stems from.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.830
- I think that the reason
that it was so weird to me

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:10.830
was because one moment I
was a fan and then suddenly

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.200
I was looked at as this
like higher up suddenly,

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.040
even when I was 14 and it was so weird

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:26.040
because I was like "I'm not
even anyone, I just make music"

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:30.750
and these kids that I
feel like I already know

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.870
suddenly like, oh, they're Billie's fans

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:34.230
and then there's Billie.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.890
And so that's why it was so weird to me

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:39.210
but I think of them as
like literally my skin,

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.810
like part of me and like
how I get through stuff

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.570
and you know, they always have my back

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.620
and like they're fans
just as much as I'm a fan,

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.050
but that doesn't make them any
less than me or anybody else.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.090
You know?

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.040
- Now one of the things

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.970
that I'm also so in love with
you for is your directing.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.080
Why did you know that you would
be the one to take control

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.640
and get your vision across?

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.300
- I mean, I've always, I've
always had the ideas already.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:11.940
I just didn't really know
that I could do them myself

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.857
for awhile, but then after
awhile I was just like,

00:03:13.857 --> 00:03:14.843
"You know what?

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.530
I want to do this," because
I think I've realized

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.750
that this is what I've
wanted to do all along

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.620
and I can actually, like
I have to prove myself

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.280
and I really had to prove myself

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.890
because who's gonna trust
a little 15 year old kid

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.970
that doesn't have any experience at all?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.230
But I did and it's been like-

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.720
- Someone did.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.900
- Yeah. The best decision ever.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.733
Ever, ever.

00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:42.160
- And kind of like, you know,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.810
do you know Pippi Longstocking?

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.184
- Yeah.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:47.413
Hell yeah.

00:03:47.413 --> 00:03:50.510
- The Go-Go's Beauty and the Beat album

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.530
and Pippi Longstocking
were like these two things

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.720
that collided in my world
when I was a little girl

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.620
right here in Los Angeles.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.830
And they both showed me
that I could do anything,

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.490
it didn't matter that I was a girl

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.840
and I didn't have to become
a man or a man hater.,

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.430
I could be all things girl,
but I could do anything.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.263
- Yeah.

00:04:10.263 --> 00:04:14.760
- And I loved how personal
you were about the marketing

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.370
and putting out of your album.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:25.370
How are you feeling about this
album being out there now?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.093
How does it feel?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.890
- It feels good.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:34.890
I was very, very, very nervous

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.733
and very worried and anxious.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:43.460
'Cause also, you know,
sophomore album is like,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.434
has more pressure than the first one,

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.490
especially if people
really liked the first one

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.230
and it's my favorite thing in the world

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:56.230
and I have so much trust and
love shoved into this project.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.880
And I mean, it's terrifying
that it's out in the world.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.360
It couldn't be scarier to me,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.360
but I'm also very happy and
pleased and hope that, you know,

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.670
people can actually listen to the lyrics

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:15.320
and actually understand them
and listen to me (chuckles)

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.820
and contribute it to their own life

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.610
and like put it in their own situations

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.690
and I hope that it helps people

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:25.500
and just makes them make
a difference in their life

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.880
and change something in their life

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.510
that's been bothering them or something

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.230
because that's what music is for.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.420
- Well, I love you.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.890
And I will be going to bed
tonight as I usually do

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.900
playing the PJ party video in my head

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.880
and usually I'm there with you girls like.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.740
- Oh my God, can we just...

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.170
Can we just be best friends, please?

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.280
- I would love it.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.850
- I love you so much.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:56.270
This is an insanely
like surreal interview.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.300
I don't know why it's a big deal for you

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.030
because it's an insanely
enormous deal for me

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:05.256
and you're Drew Barrymore so shut up.

00:06:05.256 --> 00:06:06.330
(laughing)

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.927
- Thank you guys so much.

00:06:07.927 --> 00:06:09.270
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.190
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.700
Her new album "Happier
Than Ever" is available now

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.137
and accompanied by her
cinematic concert experience,

00:06:18.137 --> 00:06:21.345
"Happier Than Ever: A Love
Letter to Los Angeles,"

00:06:21.345 --> 00:06:24.560
which is available on Disney Plus.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.490
I'm gonna say something
directly to Billie.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:30.920
You deserve to be happier than ever.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:34.240
It is a privilege to
watch you on your journey.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.450
You bring tears to my eyes
at how much I love you.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.130
Thank you for allowing me

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.281
to have a great conversation with you.

00:06:41.281 --> 00:06:43.948
(upbeat music)

